# Frontend TCA Conventions

## Reducers & state

- Use `@Reducer` and `@ObservableState`.
- Keep state Equatable/Sendable; prefer clear domain-specific names.

## Dependencies

- Inject via `@Dependency` (e.g., clipboard, fileSystem, undoManaging, mainQueue).
- Provide live/test values; avoid global singletons.

## Effects & cancellation

- Use structured concurrency; cancel in-flight effects when starting new ones.
- Surface progress via domain payloads and update state incrementally.

## Composition

- Scope child features where appropriate (see `ItemsViewFeature` → `FSItemFeature`).
- Keep parent-child callbacks narrow and typed.

